tail - print the end of buffered input

SYNOPSIS
    tail [-count] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Read up to 8191 bytes from each file or, with no file operands, from
    standard input. Print the last count lines of the bytes read. For longer
    inputs, the result is the end of that prefix. The default count is 10.
    Supply count as a positive decimal number preceded by a dash.

EXAMPLES
    tail -3 /README

SEE ALSO
    cat(1), head(1), wc(1)
